# DEBUG_AND_FIX_DISCIPLINE

Project-wide rule for **all** agents in this repository / workspace.

Canonical AI contracts:

- `docs/architecture/AI_EXECUTION_ROUTING.md`
- `docs/architecture/AI_HISTORY_PROMPT_VERSION.md`
- `docs/architecture/CONTENT_PROJECT_AI_INTEGRATION.md`
- `docs/operations/AI_DEBUG_PLAYBOOK.md`

## CORE RULE

**NEVER MAKE THE SYSTEM "RUN" BY HIDING WHY IT WAS BROKEN.**

OBSERVE FIRST.  
PROVE THE FAILING LAYER.  
REPORT ROOT CAUSE.  
FIX ONLY AUTHORIZED ROOT CAUSE.  
TEST THE CONTRACT.

---

## RULE: DEBUG TASK ≠ FIX TASK

When the user asks to: debug, investigate, trace, inspect, audit, reproduce, test, find root cause, report —

the task is **DEBUG ONLY** unless the user **explicitly** authorizes fixes.

### DEBUG MUST

- reproduce  
- collect evidence  
- identify failing layer  
- classify root cause  
- report  

### DEBUG MUST NOT

- opportunistically refactor  
- change business logic  
- reorder models  
- change free/paid policy  
- change retry limits  
- bypass validation  
- clear health merely to make a test pass  
- change workflow sequencing  
- silently fix adjacent bugs  

---

## RULE: ONLY DEBUG BLOCKERS MAY BE FIXED DURING DEBUG

Allowed **only** when the issue prevents:

- execution from running at all  
- required observability / history from being persisted  
- requested trace from being collected  

Example: duplicate routing-attempt sequence crashes persistence → minimal unblock fix allowed.

Anything else: **report first**.

---

## RULE: FINDING CLASSIFICATION

Every finding must be exactly one of:

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| A | DEBUG BLOCKER |
| B | CONFIRMED PRODUCT BUG |
| C | EXPECTED BEHAVIOR |
| D | TEST / ENVIRONMENT STATE |
| E | UNKNOWN |

Only **A. DEBUG BLOCKER** may be minimally fixed during DEBUG.

---

## RULE: FIX ONE ROOT CAUSE

For an explicitly authorized FIX task, state **before editing**:

- ROOT CAUSE  
- FAILING CONTRACT  
- RESPONSIBLE LAYER  
- EXPECTED FILES  

Then:

- smallest responsible fix  
- preserve unrelated behavior  
- add / run regression coverage  
- targeted tests  
- report behavioral impact  

Do not bundle unrelated cleanup.

---

## RULE: DO NOT FIX SYMPTOMS

Not valid product fixes unless explicitly requested:

- raise `MAX_AI_ATTEMPTS` / `MAX_FREE_ATTEMPTS`  
- reorder models to make a test pass  
- disable health  
- unlock connection permanently  
- force provider / force cost mode  
- lower validator threshold  
- swallow exception  
- retry indefinitely  
- delete state so the error disappears  

Temporary manipulation is **TEST SETUP only**. Report:

- STATE BEFORE  
- TEMPORARY CHANGE  
- WHY  
- RESULT  
- STATE AFTER  

---

## RULE: RESPECT ARCHITECTURE LAYERS

| Bug class | Fix layer |
|-----------|-----------|
| Routing eligibility | eligibility / planner |
| Budget | budget policy |
| Provider classification | classifier |
| Health scope | health layer |
| Validation | validation contract |
| History | History persistence / presenter |
| Content Project sequencing | workflow layer |

Do not weaken another layer to compensate.

---

## RULE: AI ROUTING CONTRACT

- Manual AI Center sortable order is runtime order.  
- Cost class does **not** reorder.  
- Health may skip but does not reorder.  
- Static exclusion is not Health.  
- Logical model ≠ physical route.  
- Sibling physical routes remain independent.  
- Skipped route = zero API attempts.  
- Provider success + validation failure ≠ provider failure.  

---

## RULE: OBSERVE BEFORE MODIFY

If root cause is not observable: improve debug trace first.  
Do not alter behavior based on guesses.

---

## RULE: DATABASE / DESTRUCTIVE ACTIONS

Never truncate, reset history, clear health, delete project data, run destructive migrations, or modify production-like state **without explicit user approval**.

---

## RULE: GIT SAFETY

Do not commit, push, `reset --hard`, revert unrelated edits, or clean untracked files unless explicitly requested.  
Preserve unrelated user changes.

---

## RULE: RESOURCE CONSTRAINT

Development machine is resource-constrained.

Default:

- one substantial agent  
- no parallel heavy agents  
- targeted tests first  
- no concurrent heavy PHPUnit suites  
- sequential runtime fixtures  
- avoid unnecessary rebuild / index commands  

---

## RULE: REPORT CHANGES DURING DEBUG

Every DEBUG report must include:

- OBSERVATIONS  
- ROOT CAUSES  
- CLASSIFICATION  
- CHANGES MADE DURING DEBUG  
- TEMP TEST STATE CHANGES  
- UNFIXED PRODUCT BUGS  
- NEXT RECOMMENDED FIX  

For every changed file:

- why changed  
- why it qualified as DEBUG BLOCKER  
- behavioral impact  
- regression test  
